    "title": "Liftoff! NASA's Artemis II moon rocket launches from Kennedy Space Center",
    "text": "SPACELiftoff! NASA's mighty Artemis II rocket launches, sending astronauts toward moon Rick NealeFlorida TodayApril 1, 2026Updated April 2, 2026, 9:22 a.m. ETAmerica is sending astronauts back to the moon for the first time in more than half a century.Towering taller than the Statue of Liberty, NASA's 322-foot Space Launch System rocket — featuring an orange core stage flanked by twin white solid rocket boosters — rumbled skyward off pad 39B against a blue backdrop at Kennedy Space Center while throngs of spectators watched across Florida's Space Coast.",
